<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Remediates BitLocker volumes stuck mid-encryption on the OS drive.

.DESCRIPTION
    Designed to run as SYSTEM via an Intune Proactive Remediation, on a repeating
    schedule (e.g. hourly). BitLocker decrypt/encrypt can take a long time, and
    Intune remediation scripts cannot run indefinitely, so this script is an
    IDEMPOTENT STATE MACHINE: each execution inspects current state and advances
    one step, persisting progress to a state file. Re-running it is always safe.

    Pipeline:
      1. NotStarted   -> Disable-BitLocker (stops whatever was happening, begins full decrypt)
      2. Decrypting   -> wait (log progress, exit) until FullyDecrypted
      3. Decrypted    -> read Intune/GPO-pushed FVE policy from registry, trigger an
                         MDM policy sync (so the BitLocker CSP re-applies), and as a
                         reliable fallback explicitly Enable-BitLocker with a TPM
                         protector using the policy's configured cipher
      4. Encrypting   -> wait (log progress, exit) until FullyEncrypted
      5. Encrypted    -> remove old recovery password protectors, add a brand-new one,
                         escrow it to Entra ID (BackupToAAD-BitLockerKeyProtector)
      6. AwaitingPin  -> wait for the org's separate PIN-enrollment app (deployed to
                         all devices via Intune) to add a TpmPin protector. Decryption
                         itself never needs a reboot; only PIN activation does.
      7. PendingReboot -> once a PIN protector is detected, issue a deferred/soft
                         restart notification (shutdown.exe with a countdown, not a
                         silent forced reboot) so pre-boot PIN auth activates. Re-checks
                         each run whether the device has actually rebooted since.
      8. Complete     -> no-op, exits success

.NOTES
    ASSUMPTIONS / CAVEATS - read before deploying:
      - Enables BitLocker with a TPM-only protector first (a SYSTEM-context script
        can't supply a PIN interactively). Assumes a separate, org-deployed Intune
        app enrolls the PIN afterward and adds a TpmPin protector - this script
        just waits for that protector to appear, then prompts for the reboot that
        activates it. If that app doesn't run, devices will sit in AwaitingPin.
      - Assumes hybrid Azure AD join (on-prem AD + Entra registration). Escrow
        relies on the device's own Entra device registration/certificate, which
        hybrid-joined devices have, and works under SYSTEM without user context.
